{"protocolSection":{"identificationModule":{"nctId":"NCT02172911"},"sponsorCollaboratorsModule":{"leadSponsor":{"name":"Inovio Pharmaceuticals","class":"INDUSTRY"}},"armsInterventionsModule":{"armGroups":[{"label":"Cohort I: INO-3112: Curative Intent","type":"EXPERIMENTAL","description":"Cohort I included participants with biopsy-proven, stage IB-IVB inoperable, newly diagnosed invasive cervical carcinoma associated with HPV-16 and/or HPV-18 treated with standard chemoradiation therapy with curative intent. Participants received a 4-dose series of 1.1 mL IM injection of INO-3112 followed immediately by EP with CELLECTRA™-5P.","interventionNames":["Biological: INO-3112","Device: CELLECTRA™-5P"]},{"label":"Cohort II: INO-3112: Salvage Therapy","type":"EXPERIMENTAL","description":"Cohort II included participants with persistent and/or recurrent cervical carcinoma associated with HPV-16 and/or HPV-18 who had been treated with salvage therapy (chemotherapy and/or radiation therapy). Participants received a 4-dose series of 1.1 mL IM injection of INO-3112 followed immediately by EP with CELLECTRA™-5P.","interventionNames":["Biological: INO-3112","Device: CELLECTRA™-5P"]}],"interventions":[{"type":"BIOLOGICAL","name":"INO-3112","description":"1.1 mL intramuscular (IM) injection of INO-3112 (VGX-3100 + INO-9012) was administered followed immediately by electroporation (EP) with CELLECTRA™-5P on Day 0, Week 4, Week 8, and Week 12.","armGroupLabels":["Cohort I: INO-3112: Curative Intent","Cohort II: INO-3112: Salvage Therapy"],"otherNames":["VGX-3100","INO-9012"]},{"type":"DEVICE","name":"CELLECTRA™-5P","description":"CELLECTRA™-5P was used for EP following IM delivery of INO-3112 on Day 0, Week 4, Week 8, and Week 12.","armGroupLabels":["Cohort I: INO-3112: Curative Intent","Cohort II: INO-3112: Salvage Therapy"]}]}}},
